@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`

-- Chuong I (Dieu 1-14): general provisions, the definitions of Dieu 4 above all.
-- Law 139/2025/QH15 touches Dieu 3, 6, 8, 9, 11 and 13 of this Chuong; each such provision has
-- one arm per vintage, each arm citing the source lines of the text that supplies it
-- (law08-2022-qh15.txt for V1, law139-2025-qh15 for the amendment). A provision it did not
-- touch has one arm. See law08-vintage.l4 for the dates.
-- An undated rule here does not refuse for a date before 1 January 2023 (NOTES.md, fork F2).

§ `Chuong I: Nhung quy dinh chung`

§§ `Dieu 1: scope`

-- Dieu 1(1) states what the Law regulates; Dieu 1(2) excludes four kinds of insurance.
@@q 27 29
@ref Dieu 1 (src:27-29)
`Dieu 1(1) — scope of regulation (statement; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The Law regulates the organisation and operation of insurance business, the rights and obligations of those who take part in insurance, and State management of insurance business."

@@q 30 31
@ref Dieu 1 (src:30-31)
GIVEN s IS AN `An insurance scheme`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 1(2): the Law applies to the scheme` s MEANS
    NOT (   s's `is social insurance`
         OR s's `is health insurance`
         OR s's `is deposit insurance`
         OR s's `is another kind of insurance the State provides without a business character`)

§§ `Dieu 2: those the Law applies to`

@@q 33 47
@ref Dieu 2 (src:33-47)
`Dieu 2 — persons the Law applies to (a list of addressees; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Insurers, reinsurers, agents, brokers, ancillary service providers, mutual organisations (1); foreign branches (2); foreign representative offices (3); policyholders, insured persons, beneficiaries (4); the State management body (5); other related organisations and individuals (6)."

§§ `Dieu 3: applying this Law, other laws and international custom`

-- Dieu 3(1). A later law may differ from this Law on the listed matters only if it states
-- specifically what content of this Law is applied or not applied. The Law does not say what
-- follows if it does not (fork F3), so the rule answers only whether the condition is met.
@@q 50 56
@ref Dieu 3 (src:50-56)
GIVEN l IS A `A later law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 3(1): the later law meets the condition of Dieu 3(1)` l MEANS
        NOT (l's `was issued after the Law took effect` AND l's `differs on a matter Dieu 3(1) lists`)
    OR  l's `states specifically which content is applied or not applied under this Law`

-- Dieu 3(2). The parties may agree to apply international custom in two cases; if its
-- consequence would be contrary to the basic principles of Vietnamese law, Vietnamese law applies.
@@q 57 62
@ref Dieu 3 (src:57-62)
GIVEN a IS AN `An agreement to apply international custom`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 3(2): international custom applies` a MEANS
        a's `the contract is one of insurance, reinsurance or brokerage`
    AND a's `the parties agreed to apply the custom`
    AND (   a's `at least one party is a foreign organisation or individual`
         OR (    a's `all parties are Vietnamese organisations or citizens`
             AND a's `the object of insurance or the performance of the contract is abroad`))
    AND NOT a's `applying the custom would be contrary to the basic principles of Vietnamese law`

-- Dieu 3(3) exists from V2: Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(1) adds it after Dieu 3(2). V1 has two khoan.
@@qa 24 30
@ref Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1 (src:law139-2025-qh15:24-30)
GIVEN i IS A `A would-be investor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 3(3): the person has the right to contribute capital to found, manage and control` i MEANS
    IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
    THEN     i's `the target is an insurer, reinsurer, broker, mutual organisation or foreign branch`
         AND NOT i's `has no right to found and manage an enterprise in Vietnam under the Law on Enterprises`
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 3(3) does not exist in V1: Law 08/2022/QH15 Dieu 3 has two khoan; it was added by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(1) from 1 January 2026"

§§ `Dieu 4: definitions`

-- The helpers for the kinds of insurer (Dieu 4(17)-(20), (23)).
GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`k is a doanh nghiep bao hiem (Dieu 4(17))` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a life insurer`                          THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a non-life insurer`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a health insurer`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a reinsurer`                             THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a branch of a foreign non-life insurer`  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a branch of a foreign reinsurer`         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a microinsurance mutual organisation`    THEN FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `A kind of insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`k is a foreign branch (Dieu 2(2))` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a branch of a foreign non-life insurer`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a branch of a foreign reinsurer`         THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Dieu 4(2): insurance business is done by an insurer, a foreign non-life branch or a mutual
-- organisation (not by a reinsurer or a reinsurer's branch).
@@q 69 75
@ref Dieu 4 (src:69-75)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(2): the activity is insurance business` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `carried on by`
    WHEN `a life insurer`                          THEN `the risk is accepted against premium` a
    WHEN `a non-life insurer`                      THEN `the risk is accepted against premium` a
    WHEN `a health insurer`                        THEN `the risk is accepted against premium` a
    WHEN `a branch of a foreign non-life insurer`  THEN `the risk is accepted against premium` a
    WHEN `a microinsurance mutual organisation`    THEN `the risk is accepted against premium` a
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the risk is accepted against premium` a MEANS
        a's `accepts the risk of the insured person`
    AND a's `the policyholder pays premium for it`
    AND a's `pays on the insured event as the contract agrees`

-- Dieu 4(3): reinsurance business is done by an insurer, a reinsurer or a foreign branch.
@@q 78 83
@ref Dieu 4 (src:78-83)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(3): the activity is reinsurance business` a MEANS
        (   `k is a doanh nghiep bao hiem (Dieu 4(17))` (a's `carried on by`)
         OR a's `carried on by` EQUALS `a reinsurer`
         OR `k is a foreign branch (Dieu 2(2))` (a's `carried on by`))
    AND a's `receives a reinsurance premium from another insurer, reinsurer, branch, foreign insurer, foreign reinsurer or foreign insurance organisation`
    AND a's `undertakes to compensate for the liabilities taken`

-- Dieu 4(4): ceding of reinsurance, by the same actors.
@@q 84 89
@ref Dieu 4 (src:84-89)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(4): the activity is ceding of reinsurance` a MEANS
        (   `k is a doanh nghiep bao hiem (Dieu 4(17))` (a's `carried on by`)
         OR `k is a foreign branch (Dieu 2(2))` (a's `carried on by`)
         OR a's `carried on by` EQUALS `a reinsurer`)
    AND a's `transfers part of the liability taken in reinsurance to another insurer, reinsurer, branch or foreign body`
    AND a's `pays a ceding premium for the transfer`

-- Dieu 4(5): agency activity: one or more of six acts, under the authorisation of an insurer,
-- a foreign non-life branch or a mutual organisation.
@@q 90 95
@ref Dieu 4 (src:90-95)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(5): the activity is insurance agency activity` a MEANS
        a's `acts under the authorisation of an insurer, a branch or a mutual organisation`
    AND (   a's `advises on insurance products`
         OR a's `introduces insurance products`
         OR a's `offers insurance products for sale`
         OR a's `arranges the making of insurance contracts`
         OR a's `collects premium`
         OR a's `collects dossiers for claims settlement`)

-- Dieu 4(6): brokerage. The sentence names two things after "la hoat dong"; it is read as
-- either one making the activity brokerage (fork F4).
@@q 96 100
@ref Dieu 4 (src:96-100)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(6): the activity is insurance brokerage activity` a MEANS
        a's `provides information and advice to the policyholder on types, products, programmes, terms, premium or insurers`
    OR  a's `negotiates, arranges the making of or performs insurance or reinsurance contracts`

-- Dieu 4(7). Ancillary services are those five; what the insurer does for itself is not one.
@@q 101 106
@ref Dieu 4 (src:101-106)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(7): the activity is an ancillary insurance service` s MEANS
        (   s's `is advice on insurance programmes, products, risk management or loss prevention`
         OR s's `identifies, classifies and assesses the nature and degree of insurable risk`
         OR s's `collects and analyses statistics, computes premium, reserves, capital or solvency`
         OR s's `determines the condition, cause and extent of a loss and apportions liability`
         OR s's `helps a policyholder, insured person, beneficiary or insurer with claims procedures`)
    AND NOT s's `is done by the insurer, reinsurer, branch or mutual organisation itself for its own business`

-- Dieu 4(8)-(12): the five ancillary services, one rule each.
@@q 107 108
@ref Dieu 4 (src:107-108)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(8): the activity is advice (tu van)` s MEANS
    s's `is advice on insurance programmes, products, risk management or loss prevention`

@@q 111 113
@ref Dieu 4 (src:111-113)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(9): the activity is insurance risk assessment` s MEANS
    s's `identifies, classifies and assesses the nature and degree of insurable risk`

@@q 114 118
@ref Dieu 4 (src:114-118)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(10): the activity is actuarial work (tinh toan bao hiem)` s MEANS
    s's `collects and analyses statistics, computes premium, reserves, capital or solvency`

@@q 119 121
@ref Dieu 4 (src:119-121)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(11): the activity is insurance loss adjustment (giam dinh ton that)` s MEANS
    s's `determines the condition, cause and extent of a loss and apportions liability`

@@q 122 125
@ref Dieu 4 (src:122-125)
GIVEN s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(12): the activity is claims support` s MEANS
    s's `helps a policyholder, insured person, beneficiary or insurer with claims procedures`

-- Dieu 4(1): insurance business activity is the six activities. An activity is within it if it
-- is one of insurance, reinsurance, ceding, agency, brokerage or an ancillary service.
@@q 65 68
@ref Dieu 4 (src:65-68)
GIVEN a IS AN `An activity`
      s IS AN `An ancillary activity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(1): the activity is insurance business activity (hoat dong kinh doanh bao hiem)` a s MEANS
        `Dieu 4(2): the activity is insurance business` a
    OR  `Dieu 4(3): the activity is reinsurance business` a
    OR  `Dieu 4(4): the activity is ceding of reinsurance` a
    OR  `Dieu 4(5): the activity is insurance agency activity` a
    OR  `Dieu 4(6): the activity is insurance brokerage activity` a
    OR  `Dieu 4(7): the activity is an ancillary insurance service` s

-- Dieu 4(13)-(15) and (22): what a product covers. The three types overlap in fact; a cover may
-- be more than one (a product combining life and health cover is both).
@@q 126 127
@ref Dieu 4 (src:126-127)
GIVEN c IS A `A cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(13): the cover is life insurance` c MEANS
    c's `covers the insured person living or dying`

@@q 128 129
@ref Dieu 4 (src:128-129)
GIVEN c IS A `A cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(14): the cover is non-life insurance` c MEANS
    c's `covers damage to property and other losses` OR c's `covers civil liability to a third person`

@@q 130 131
@ref Dieu 4 (src:130-131)
GIVEN c IS A `A cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(15): the cover is health insurance` c MEANS
    c's `covers injury, accident, illness, disease or health care`

@@q 159 160
@ref Dieu 4 (src:159-160)
GIVEN c IS A `A cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(22): the cover is microinsurance` c MEANS
    c's `is directed at low-income individuals or households` AND c's `protects against risks to life, health and property`

-- Dieu 4(17)-(21), (23): the kinds of enterprise.
@@q 138 144
@ref Dieu 4 (src:138-144)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` e MEANS
        e's `established, organised and operating under this Law and other related laws`
    AND e's `operates to carry on insurance business, reinsurance business and ceding`

GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a life insurer` e MEANS
    `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` e AND e's `carries on life insurance`

GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a non-life insurer` e MEANS
    `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` e AND e's `carries on non-life insurance`

GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a health insurer` e MEANS
    `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` e AND e's `carries on health insurance`

@@q 145 147
@ref Dieu 4 (src:145-147)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(18): the enterprise is a reinsurer` e MEANS
        e's `established, organised and operating under this Law and other related laws`
    AND e's `operates to carry on reinsurance business and ceding`

@@q 148 151
@ref Dieu 4 (src:148-151)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(19): the enterprise is a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` e MEANS
        e's `is a dependent unit of a foreign insurer or reinsurer`
    AND e's `the foreign body is a non-life insurer`
    AND NOT e's `is a legal person`
    AND e's `the foreign insurer or reinsurer guarantees and answers for all its obligations in Vietnam`

@@q 152 155
@ref Dieu 4 (src:152-155)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(20): the enterprise is a branch of a foreign reinsurer` e MEANS
        e's `is a dependent unit of a foreign insurer or reinsurer`
    AND e's `the foreign body is a reinsurer`
    AND NOT e's `is a legal person`
    AND e's `the foreign insurer or reinsurer guarantees and answers for all its obligations in Vietnam`

@@q 156 158
@ref Dieu 4 (src:156-158)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(21): the enterprise is an insurance broker` e MEANS
        e's `established, organised and operating under this Law and other related laws`
    AND e's `operates to carry on insurance brokerage activity`

@@q 161 166
@ref Dieu 4 (src:161-166)
GIVEN e IS AN `An enterprise`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(23): the organisation is a microinsurance mutual organisation` e MEANS
        e's `is a legal person`
    AND e's `keeps independent accounts`
    AND e's `was founded by members or a body representing members`
    AND e's `operates without a profit purpose, for mutual support among members`
    AND e's `is voluntary, financially autonomous and answerable only within the assets formed from microinsurance`

-- Dieu 4(16), (24)-(29): the contract and its parties.
@@q 132 137
@ref Dieu 4 (src:132-137)
GIVEN c IS A `A contract arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` c MEANS
        c's `is an agreement between the policyholder and the insurer, branch or mutual organisation`
    AND c's `the policyholder must pay premium under it`
    AND c's `the insurer, branch or mutual organisation must compensate or pay as agreed under it`

@@q 167 169
@ref Dieu 4 (src:167-169)
GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` r MEANS
    r's `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation` AND r's `pays the insurance premium`

@@q 170 172
@ref Dieu 4 (src:170-172)
GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` r MEANS
    r's `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract`

@@q 175 177
@ref Dieu 4 (src:175-177)
GIVEN r IS A `A role in a contract`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` r MEANS
    r's `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees`

@@q 178 181
@ref Dieu 4 (src:178-181)
GIVEN o IS AN `An occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` o MEANS
        o's `is an objective event`
    AND o's `was agreed by the parties or is provided by law`
    AND o's `obliges the insurer, branch or mutual organisation to compensate or pay under the contract when it occurs`

@@q 182 185
@ref Dieu 4 (src:182-185)
GIVEN p IS A `A payment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` p MEANS
    p's `is made by the policyholder to the insurer, branch or mutual organisation` AND p's `is required by law or agreed by the parties in the contract`

@@q 186 190
@ref Dieu 4 (src:186-190)
GIVEN c IS A `A contract arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 4(29): the arrangement is co-insurance (dong bao hiem)` c MEANS
        c's `several insurers or branches of foreign non-life insurers agreed to make it with the policyholder in one contract`
    AND c's `they take premium and compensate or pay in the ratio agreed in the contract`

§§ `Dieu 5: policy`

@@q 192 204
@ref Dieu 5 (src:192-204)
`Dieu 5 — State policy to develop insurance business (policy statements; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The State protects the lawful rights of insurance participants and insurance businesses (1); and encourages research, technology (2), reinvestment (3), and agricultural, forestry, fishery, microinsurance and social-security products (4)."

§§ `Dieu 6: principles of supplying and using insurance services`

-- Dieu 6(1). A person in Vietnam may take insurance only from a licensed insurer, branch or
-- mutual organisation, unless the insurance is a cross-border service under a treaty.
@@q 208 213
@ref Dieu 6 (src:208-213)
GIVEN p IS A `A purchase of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 6(1): the purchase conforms` p MEANS
        NOT p's `the buyer is an organisation or individual in Vietnam`
    OR  p's `the seller holds a licence to establish and operate in Vietnam`
    OR  p's `the insurance is a cross-border service under an international treaty to which Vietnam is a member`

-- Dieu 6(2). The Government regulates three cross-border services in V1 and V2; Law 139/2025/QH15
-- Dieu 2(6) strikes the ancillary one from 1 July 2026 (V3).
@@q 214 217
@@qa 333 334
@ref Dieu 6 (src:214-217; src:law139-2025-qh15:333-334)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A cross-border service`
`Dieu 6(2): the cross-border services the Government is to regulate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V3`
           THEN LIST `cross-border insurance`, `cross-border insurance brokerage`
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN LIST `cross-border insurance`, `cross-border insurance brokerage`, `cross-border ancillary insurance service`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

-- The Government's detailed rules are not among the sources: encoded as a refusal.
GIVEN s IS A `A cross-border service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 6(2): the Government's detailed rules on the cross-border service` s MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 6(2) delegates the detail of cross-border services to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 7: types of insurance`

@@q 219 222
@ref Dieu 7 (src:219-222)
`Dieu 7(1) — the three types of insurance are life, health and non-life (carried by the enumeration A type of insurance in law08-nouns.l4; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "(a) life insurance; (b) health insurance; (c) non-life insurance."

@@q 223 224
@ref Dieu 7 (src:223-224)
GIVEN t IS A `A type of insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 7(2): the Government's list of insurance lines for the type` t MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 7(2) delegates the lines (nghiep vu) of each type to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 8: compulsory insurance`

-- Dieu 8(1)-(2). The product is compulsory insurance if it is one of the four listed. The
-- phrase in (c) is "hoat dong dau tu xay dung" in V1 and, by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(1), "hoat
-- dong xay dung" from V2. Whether the second is wider is not given in the sources (fork F5): the
-- facts are two separate inputs.
@@q 226 233
@@qa 321 322
@ref Dieu 8 (src:226-233; src:law139-2025-qh15:321-322)
GIVEN p IS A `A product for the purposes of compulsory insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` p MEANS
        p's `is civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners`
    OR  p's `is compulsory fire and explosion insurance`
    OR  (   IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
            THEN p's `is insurance in construction activity`
            ELSE p's `is insurance in construction investment activity`)
    OR  p's `is compulsory under another law and meets Dieu 8(1)`

-- Dieu 8(3)-(4).
@@q 236 243
@ref Dieu 8 (src:236-243)
GIVEN s IS A `A sale of compulsory insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 8(3): the buyer is bound to buy compulsory insurance` s MEANS
    s's `the buyer is within the class that must buy it`

GIVEN s IS A `A sale of compulsory insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` s MEANS
        s's `the seller is permitted to offer it`
    AND s's `the buyer meets the conditions the law sets for buying`
    AND s's `the seller refused to sell`

-- Dieu 8(5). The Government fixes the conditions, the premium and the minimum sum insured.
@@q 244 245
@ref Dieu 8 (src:244-245)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 8(5): the premium of compulsory insurance` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 8(5) delegates the premium of compulsory insurance to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`Dieu 8(5): the minimum sum insured of compulsory insurance` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 8(5) delegates the minimum sum insured of compulsory insurance to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 8(5): the conditions of compulsory insurance are met` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 8(5) delegates the conditions of compulsory insurance to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 9: prohibited acts`

-- Dieu 9(1)-(5). Dieu 9(3): agency and ancillary services in V1 and V2; Law 139/2025/QH15
-- Dieu 2(6) removes the ancillary words from 1 July 2026 (V3).
@@q 247 261
@@qa 333 334
@ref Dieu 9 (src:247-261; src:law139-2025-qh15:333-334)
GIVEN a IS AN `An act in insurance business`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 9: the act is prohibited` a MEANS
        (a's `is insurance, reinsurance, ceding or brokerage business` AND a's `is done without a licence to establish and operate`)
    OR  (a's `is insurance, reinsurance, ceding or brokerage business` AND a's `is done outside the scope of the licence`)
    OR  (    (   a's `is insurance agency activity`
              OR (    NOT `the rules in force are those of V3`
                  AND a's `is an ancillary insurance service`))
         AND a's `the actor does not meet the conditions of law to do it`)
    OR  a's `is colluding with a beneficiary to settle a claim unlawfully`
    OR  a's `is forging documents or deliberately falsifying information in a claim dossier`
    OR  a's `is forging documents or deliberately falsifying information to refuse a claim after the insured event`
    OR  a's `is causing loss to one's own property or health to get insurance benefits`
    OR  a's `is threatening or coercing the making of an insurance contract`

§§ `Dieu 10: social-professional organisations`

@@q 263 273
@ref Dieu 10 (src:263-273)
`Dieu 10 — social-professional organisations (duties of an association; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "They are set up and operate under the law on associations, must comply with the insurance law and are supervised by the Ministry of Finance (1); they issue codes of professional ethics and standards and help spread the law (2)."

§§ `Dieu 11: the database on insurance business`

@@q 275 278
@ref Dieu 11 (src:275-278)
`Dieu 11(1) — the State invests in the database; the Ministry of Finance builds, manages and runs it (no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The State invests in building the database; the Ministry of Finance is responsible for building, managing and operating it."

-- Dieu 11(2).
@@q 279 284
@ref Dieu 11 (src:279-284)
GIVEN u IS A `A use of database information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 11(2): the supplier has supplied the information the database needs` u MEANS
        u's `the supplier is an insurer, reinsurer, branch, broker, ancillary provider or mutual organisation`
    AND u's `supplied information on the policyholder, insured person, object, agent and other related information`

-- Dieu 11(3). The safety limb is "an toan thong tin" in V1 and, by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(2),
-- "an ninh mang" from V2.
@@q 285 292
@@qa 324 324
@ref Dieu 11 (src:285-292; src:law139-2025-qh15:324)
GIVEN u IS A `A use of database information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 11(3): the collection, use, storage and supply of database information complies` u MEANS
        u's `ensured confidentiality`
    AND (   IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
            THEN u's `ensured cybersecurity`
            ELSE u's `ensured information safety`)
    AND u's `complied with the law on privacy, personal, family and business secrets`
    AND u's `used the information for the purpose supplied`
    AND (   NOT u's `gave it to a third party`
         OR u's `the policyholder or insured person agreed`
         OR u's `a law provides for the supply`)

@@q 293 294
@ref Dieu 11 (src:293-294)
`Dieu 11(4) — the database is connected to other national and specialised databases (no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The database is connected with the national databases and other specialised databases."

@@q 295 300
@ref Dieu 11 (src:295-300)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 11(5): the Government's detailed rules on the database` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 11(5) delegates the building, collection, use, storage and supply of the database and its connection to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 12: information technology`

@@q 303 312
@ref Dieu 12 (src:303-312)
`Dieu 12(1) — the purposes of applying information technology (statement; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Application of information technology aims to raise efficiency (a) and to modernise statistics and reporting, cut procedures and build systems against fraud (b)."

@@q 313 316
@ref Dieu 12 (src:313-316)
`Dieu 12(2) — application must comply with this Law and the laws on electronic transactions, information technology, cybersecurity and anti-money-laundering (cross-reference to other laws; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Application of information technology must comply with this Law and the other laws named."

@@q 317 318
@ref Dieu 12 (src:317-318)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 12(3): the Government's rules on new matters in applying information technology` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 12(3) delegates new matters of applying information technology to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 13: requirements on the information technology system`

-- The minimum requirements. The cybersecurity limb reads "an ninh mang, an toan thong tin mang"
-- in V1 and, by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(5), "an ninh mang" alone from V2.
@@q 321 333
@@qa 332 332
@ref Dieu 13 (src:321-333; src:law139-2025-qh15:332)
GIVEN s IS AN `An information technology system`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 13: the system meets the minimum requirements` s MEANS
        s's `has servers, software and technical solutions to update, count, process and store information`
    AND s's `meets cybersecurity requirements`
    AND (   IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
            THEN TRUE
            ELSE s's `meets network information safety requirements`)
    AND s's `eases the running, risk control and supervision`
    AND s's `has disaster recovery and continuity solutions`

§§ `Dieu 14: supplying insurance online`

@@q 335 340
@ref Dieu 14 (src:335-340)
GIVEN o IS AN `An online offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 14(1): the offeror may supply insurance services and products online` o MEANS
        o's `the offeror is an insurer, branch or mutual organisation`
    OR  o's `the offeror is an insurance agent`
    OR  o's `the offeror is an insurance broker`

@@q 347 348
@ref Dieu 14 (src:347-348)
GIVEN o IS AN `An online offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 14(2)(b): the agent's online offer is within the agency contract` o MEANS
    (NOT o's `the offeror is an insurance agent`) OR o's `the offer is within the scope of the agency contract`

@@q 349 354
@ref Dieu 14 (src:349-354)
GIVEN o IS AN `An online offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 14(2)(c): the offeror is liable to the policyholder` o MEANS
        (   o's `the offeror is an insurer, branch or mutual organisation`
         OR o's `the offeror is an insurance agent`
         OR o's `the offeror is an insurance broker`)
    AND o's `the policyholder's rights were affected`

@@q 355 357
@ref Dieu 14 (src:355-357)
GIVEN o IS AN `An online offer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 14(2)(d): the information given online satisfies Dieu 22` o MEANS
    o's `the contract party gave truthful and accurate information as Dieu 22 requires`

@@q 358 358
@ref Dieu 14 (src:358)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 14(3): the Minister of Finance's detailed rules on supplying insurance online` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 14(3) delegates the detail to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"
